#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:30
msgctxt "@title title of the dialog"
msgid "About Bug Reporting"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:43
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "Information about bug reporting"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:45
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "You can help us improve this software by filing a bug report."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:47
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "<note>It is safe to close this dialog. If you do not want to, you do not have to file a bug report.</note>"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:49
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "In order to generate a useful bug report we need some information about both the crash and your system. (Also, you may need to install some debug packages.)"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:53
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "Bug Reporting Assistant Steps Guide"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:55
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "This assistant will guide you through the crash reporting process of the KDE Bug Reports Database Site. All the information you enter to the bug report must be in English, if possible, as KDE is developed internationally."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:61
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "Crash Information"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:63
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "This page will generate a backtrace of the crash. This is information that tells the developers where the application crashed. If the crash information is not detailed enough, you may need to install some debug packages and reload it. You can find more information about backtraces, what they mean, and how they are useful at <link>%1</link>"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:69
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "Once you get a useful trace (or if you do not want to install the missing packages) you can continue."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:73
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "What do you know about the crash"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:75
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "In this page you need to answer some questions about the crash context and if you are willing to help the developers in the future if it is needed. This means you will need to open a KDE Bug tracking system account."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:79
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "If you can, describe the crash context, the details of what you were doing when the application crashed. You can mention: documents that you were using (and their type/format), actions you were taking in or outside the application, web sites you were browsing, other strange things you noticed before or after the crash, and so on."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:87
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "Conclusions"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:89
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "Using the quality of the crash information gathered previously, and your answers on the previous page, the assistant will tell you if the crash is worth reporting or not."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:92
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "If the crash is worth reporting, and the application is supported in the KDE bug tracking system, you can click <interface>Next</interface>. However if it is not supported you will need to directly contact the maintainer of the application."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:96
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "If the crash is listed as being not worth reporting, you can still manually report the bug if you want to."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:100 drkonqibugreport.cpp:89
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "KDE Bug Tracking System Login"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:102
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "As we may need to contact you in the future to ask for further information and we need to keep track of the bug reports, you need to have an account on the KDE bug tracking system. If you do not have one, you can create one here: <link>%1</link>"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:107
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "Then you can write your username and password and press the Login button. Once you are authenticated, you can press Next to continue."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:110
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "The KWallet dialog may appear when pressing Login to save your password in the KWallet password system. Also, it will prompt you for the KWallet password upon loading to autocomplete the data if you use this assistant again."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:116 drkonqibugreport.cpp:98
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "Bug Report Keywords"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:118
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "In this step you need to write at least four (4) words to identify the crash. You can use the application name, or write a little sentence about the crash or the context. This text will be used to search for similar crashes already reported in the database, to help you and others find them later. Also, this text can be used as the title of the future bug report. You can change this title later."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:124 aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:150
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "<note>You should write in English.</note>"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:127
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "Bug Report Possible Duplicate list"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:130
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "This is an optional step."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:131
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "This page will search the bug report database for similar crashes which are possibly duplicates of your bug. If there are similar bug reports found, you can double click on them to show their details. Then, read the current bug report information so you can check if the situations are similar and you can tentatively mark your crash as a duplicate of that report."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:137
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "If not enough possible duplicates are found, or you did not find a similar report, then you can force the search for more bug reports (only if the date range is not reached.)"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:140
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "Do not worry if you cannot find a similar bug report or you do not know what to look at. The bug report database maintainers will look at it later. It is better to file a duplicate then to not file at all."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:146
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "Details of the Bug report"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:148
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "In this case you need to write a title and description of the crash context. Explain as best you can."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:153 drkonqibugreport.cpp:124
msgctxt "@title"
msgid "Send Crash Report"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:155
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "This page will send the bug report to the bug tracking system and it will notify you when it is done. Then, it will show the URL of the bug report in the KDE bug tracking system, so that you can look at the report later."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk
#: aboutbugreportingdialog.cpp:159
msgctxt "@info/rich"
msgid "If the process fails, you can click <interface>Retry</interface> to try sending the bug report again."
msgstr ""

